# The typing of an application whose function may be a Scott value. The
# application rule of hindley_milner_unions (unions_application_typed) unifies
# the function's type with function_type tx r; a Scott value eliminated
# directly, xs n (λh t. a), has a structure as its type, and the unify node of
# a structure and a function type is united with both (unions_unify_*), so
# the structure and the function type become one class and the
# representation of the value is refuted (prolog_backend_shapes). This module
# types an application by applied_type tf tx instead, which stays until tf's
# class holds a shape: a function type gives its result, its parameter unified
# with tx; a structure gives the eliminator of its alternatives, each arm
# unified with the function of its alternative's fields to a result fresh for
# the elimination. No unify node of a structure and a function type is
# written, whichever of the two the class of tf holds first. It replaces
# unions_application_typed in a type check that does not use it.
#
# A value whose type has no structure, a parameter only eliminated, as xs n
# (λh t. a), is given one by its eliminations: for each shape of the
# backend's representations that a candidacy of prolog_backend_shapes or
# binary_wren_shapes reads (the unary naturals': a second alternative of one
# field; the lists': of two fields; the binary naturals': three alternatives,
# the second and third of one field each), an application chain of that many
# arms whose arms' types are functions of that many fields marks the value's
# type v with eliminated_as v s, s the structure of those fields. Where an
# elimination reads as two shapes (a list's cons arm, a function of two
# fields, is also a function of one field returning a function), both are
# marked: an ambiguous typing keeps every reading as a candidate, each
# refuted by the type's own structure and repelled at the call where it
# fails, the extraction choosing among the rest by cost. v is unified with the
# mark, never with s: a structure written out is one class for every v that
# writes it, so unifying would unite the types of values that share nothing
# but a shape. A candidacy of s then reaches v (wren_scott_candidate_through_elimination),
# and the refutations and repellers of prolog_backend_shapes act on v as on
# any candidate. The booleans' shape, two arms of no field, is not read: every
# application of two arguments has it.
#
# Every lemma is an equation of the zero universe, both sides top up to
# contextual equivalence, but wren_scott_application_typed, which is
# absorption. A lemma whose result is one of its metavariables X writes
# unify X and its left side, never X alone, which a term out of the zero
# universe would make unequal to the left side; the unions of
# hindley_milner_unions unite X's class with it.
